<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomebamba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tumebamba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomebamba was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> city in the southern highlands of Ecuador, built on the site of the Cañari centre of Guapondelig after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupac-inca-yupanqui">Túpac Inca Yupanqui</a>'s conquest of the region. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huayna-capac">Huayna Capac</a>, said to have been born there, made it a northern capital of the empire, with palaces and temples. It was ruined during the Inca civil war, and Spanish Cuenca was founded on the site in 1557.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomebamba.jpg" alt="Tomebamba" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Micah MacAllen · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pumapungo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
